d or ahead, or a shift in Latino turnout dynamics, would move this back to a pure tossup.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["Incumbent Monica De La Cruz (R) is running."]}, "overview": "First-term Republican Monica De La Cruz defends a South Texas district that leaned Republican by seven points in 2024, but Democrat Bobby Pulido, a well-known Tejano singer, has made the race one of the most watched in the country. Pulido has raised nearly $3 million with outside groups supporting him, while De La Cruz holds a cash edge. Recent polls from September show Pulido ahead by five to thirteen points, though several were conducted by Democratic-leaning pollsters. Expert raters are split: most call it a tossup, while others lean either direction, and two rate it a Democratic flip. Prediction markets on Kalshi and Polymarket price Pulido near 80 percent, well above the tossup consensus. The race is a test of whether Republican gains with Latino voters in South Texas hold or reverse.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.4454, "margin": -0.75}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.6234, "margin": 1.5}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.6548, "margin": 2.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.6308, "margin": 1.5}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.5679, "margin": 1.5}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.6942, "margin": 3.5}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.6077, "margin": 1.5}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.6479, "margin": 2.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.7065, "margin": 3.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.6601, "margin": 2.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.6541, "margin": 2.0}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.6766, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.7121, "margin": 3.0}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.6611, "margin": 3.0}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.6572, "margin": 3.0}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.6619, "margin": 3.0}, {"date": "2026-10-08", "p_dem": 0.6805, "margin": 3.0}, {"date": "2026-10-09", "p_dem": 0.6513, "ma